{color.GG}Setcursor {color.N}changes the terminal cursor appearance using predefined cursor styles.

Usage: {color.GG}setcursor {color.CC}<style>{color.N}

Available style:
    {color.R}- {color.GG}default{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}block{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}blink-block{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}line{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}blink-line{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}underline{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}blink-underline{color.N}

Example:
    {color.R}- {color.GG}setcursor {color.CC}block{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}setcursor {color.CC}blink-line{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}setcursor {color.CC}default{color.N}